    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I need help writing a rejection email. We had a candidate, Marcus, who made it all the way to the final interview for our Senior Dev role here in Austin. He's really talented and had great technical skills, but we decided to go with someone who had a bit more experience with our specific cloud architecture. I want the email to be professional and kind because he was a great guy, but we need to be firm that the decision is final. Can you draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a draft rejection email that balances professionalism with kindness:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you regarding the Senior Developer position at our Austin office. We were truly impressed by your technical skills and the enthusiasm you brought to the final interview. Unfortunately, after careful consideration, we have decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience aligns more closely with our specific cloud architecture needs.\n\nPlease know that this decision was not made lightly, and we were genuinely impressed by your qualifications and potential. However, we have to prioritize the best fit for our team, and this candidate's experience was a better match for our current requirements.\n\nI want to emphasize that this decision is final, and we appreciate the time and effort you invested in our interview process. We're grateful for the opportunity to have met you and appreciate your interest in joining our team.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out. We wish you the best of luck in your job search and hope our paths will cross again in the future.\n\nBest regards,\n[Your Name]\n\nThis email aims to convey a sense of appreciation for Marcus's qualifications and a genuine regret that we couldn't move forward with him. The phrase \"we have to prioritize the best",
