      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start. I'm worried it might sound a little bit too generic or \"templatey\" though. Could you try making it sound a bit more personal and warm? Like, acknowledge that we really enjoyed the conversation and that it was a tough call, without losing that firm boundary that we aren't reversing the decision.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised draft that aims to add a bit more warmth and personality to the email:\n\nDear Marcus,\n\nI wanted to personally reach out to you and express my gratitude for the incredible conversation we had during your final interview for the Senior Developer role at our Austin office. You truly impressed us with your technical expertise and passion for innovation, and we were delighted to learn more about your experience and interests.\n\nI want to acknowledge that this decision was far from easy, and we're still kicking ourselves for not being able to find a better fit for our team. However, after careful consideration, we've decided to move forward with another candidate whose experience aligns more closely with our specific cloud architecture needs. Please know that this decision was not a reflection on your abilities or potential – you would be a fantastic addition to any team, and we have no doubt you'll find an amazing opportunity soon.\n\nI want to thank you again for taking the time to speak with us and for sharing your vision with us. We were genuinely charmed by your enthusiasm and energy, and we're grateful for the chance to have met you. We're confident that you'll continue to excel in your career and make a lasting impact in the industry.\n\nIf you have any questions or concerns",
      "source": "target",
